<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21104] Activating an idle OSC import leaves it invalid, I/O gets EIO</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21104</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When a client OSC import has disconnected because of idle_timeout&lt;br/&gt;
(state IDLE), deactivating and then activating it leaves the import&lt;br/&gt;
invalid, and I/O to that OST fails with EIO:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;client# lctl set_param osc.lustre-OST0000-osc-*.idle_timeout=10
(wait until the OST0000 import state is IDLE)
client# lctl set_param osc.lustre-OST0000-osc-*.active=0
client# lctl set_param osc.lustre-OST0000-osc-*.active=1
client# touch /mnt/lustre/f    # f has its stripe on OST0000
touch: setting times of '/mnt/lustre/f': Input/output error&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
